<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rao Maldeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1511–1562</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Maldeo Rathore</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rao Maldeo was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> ruler of Marwar from 1532 to 1562, under whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> became the strongest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> state in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. He conquered much of the surrounding region, including Nagaur, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a> and Bikaner. In 1544 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sher-shah-suri">Sher Shah Suri</a> defeated his army at Sammel, and he later recovered his capital but never regained his earlier dominance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rao-maldeo.jpg" alt="Rao Maldeo" width="320" height="595" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H0900-L185162829.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
